## The SACRED Workflow

Every code change follows these steps. **Never skip a step.**

```
 1. SPEC CHECK     — Read current spec / acceptance criteria
 2. BRANCH         — Feature branch BEFORE writing code
 3. PLAN           — Plan Mode if 3+ files affected
 4. IMPLEMENT      — Only what's needed for acceptance criteria
 5. FORMAT         — [FORMAT_COMMAND]
 6. LINT           — [LINT_COMMAND]
 7. BUILD          — [BUILD_COMMAND] must succeed
 8. TEST           — [TEST_COMMAND] + manual verification
 9. AUDIT          — Privacy / security spot-check (if applicable)
10. VERIFY         — Return to spec, mark each criterion ✅ ⚠️ ❌
10.5 NFT CHECK     — When triggered (new dep, pre-release, new route)
11. COMMIT         — Only after full verification
12. UPDATE DOCS    — MANDATORY immediate post-commit (see below)
```

### Step 12: Post-Commit Documentation Updates (Non-Negotiable)

After every commit, **immediately** update these files (or explicitly confirm "unchanged"):

a) **planning/BACKLOG.md** — Update item status, mark acceptance criteria, note commit hash
b) **planning/LESSONS_LEARNED.md** — Add any new lessons (or confirm "none this session")
c) **CHANGELOG.md** — Entry under `[Unreleased]` for every feature/fix/security change
d) **planning/SERVICES.md** — If any new external service or tier change
e) **README.md** — If any user-facing features or setup changed
f) **MEMORY.md** — Sync with current state, update "Next Up"

---

## Session Handoff Protocol (MANDATORY before /clear)

At the end of EVERY session, complete these steps:

1. Update `## Next Up` section in BACKLOG.md (single source of truth for resuming cold)
2. Format: `- **[ITEM-ID]**: [enough detail to resume cold]`
3. Mark next planned item as 🚧 IN PROGRESS
4. Update `planning/LESSONS_LEARNED.md` — add any new lessons (or confirm "none this session")
5. Update `CHANGELOG.md` — entry under `[Unreleased]` (or confirm "none this session")
6. Update `README.md` — if any user-facing changes (or confirm "unchanged")
7. Update `planning/SERVICES.md` — if any new service or tier change (or confirm "unchanged")
8. Update `MEMORY.md` — sync "Next Up" and any new patterns; remove stale entries
9. Craft next-session kickoff prompt — ready-to-paste message for Chief
10. Push to remote — `git push origin [branch]` if any commits this session
11. Exit with `/clear`

